{"events":[{"id":23260,"global_id":"thereser.org?id=23260","global_id_lineage":["thereser.org?id=23260"],"author":"13","status":"publish","date":"2026-05-01 09:00:18","date_utc":"2026-05-01 16:00:18","modified":"2026-04-27 13:06:34","modified_utc":"2026-04-27 20:06:34","url":"https:\/\/thereser.org\/event\/roger-mcguinn-an-evening-of-songs-stories\/","rest_url":"https:\/\/thereser.org\/wp-json\/tribe\/events\/v1\/events\/23260","title":"Roger McGuinn: An Evening of Songs &#038; Stories","description":"<p>The pioneer of folk-rock and the unmistakable voice behind some of the most influential music of the 20th century, Roger McGuinn, is bringing his legendary storytelling and signature 12-string Rickenbacker sound to Patricia Reser Center for the Arts September 22nd, 2026.<\/p>\n<p>As the founder and frontman of The Byrds, McGuinn didn&#8217;t just play music; he helped invent a genre. From the jangly, celestial heights of &#8220;Eight Miles High&#8221; to the definitive folk-rock anthem &#8220;Mr. Tambourine Man,&#8221; McGuinn\u2019s influence is woven into the very fabric of American rock and roll.<\/p>\n<p>An Evening of Stories and Songs<\/p>\n<p>This intimate performance offers fans a rare journey through the history of rock music. Armed with his guitar and a lifetime of experiences, McGuinn delivers a format that is part concert and part masterclass. The setlist spans his storied career.<\/p>","excerpt":"","slug":"roger-mcguinn-an-evening-of-songs-stories","image":{"url":"https:\/\/thereser.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/04\/Roger-McGuinn-2280-x-1536.png","id":23264,"extension":"png","width":2280,"height":1536,"filesize":2164100,"sizes":{"medium":{"width":300,"height":202,"mime-type":"image\/png","filesize":75109,"url":"https:\/\/thereser.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/04\/Roger-McGuinn-2280-x-1536-300x202.png"},"large":{"width":1024,"height":690,"mime-type":"image\/png","filesize":593186,"url":"https:\/\/thereser.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/04\/Roger-McGu